# "Tap two untapped artifacts you control" needs two: with only a Mox Ruby (the Tethermage itself is a creature, not an
# artifact) the ability is not offered at all (CR 118.3), so the refusal holds and no counters are put on it. The three
# lands pay for the Tethermage; the one Mox is the only artifact on the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Forest
Tenured Tethermage
Mountain
Forest
Forest
Forest x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Opt x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tenured Tethermage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose()
! Bot1.Battlefield.Tenured Tethermage.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Tenured Tethermage.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
